Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(tests): patch requests at mcp_nixos.caches, not
 sources.base
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ChannelCache imports `requests` as its own module-level name in
mcp_nixos.caches, so patching `mcp_nixos.sources.base.requests.*` in
test_discover_channels / test_discover_skips_zero_count_aliases /
test_discover_returns_empty_on_api_error did not intercept the actual
HTTP calls — the tests could hit the real Elasticsearch backend.
Repatch at `mcp_nixos.caches.requests` so the mocks bind where the
symbol is used.

Also generalize the example alias in copilot-instructions.md from the
concrete `latest-48-nixos-25.11` to `latest-<gen>-nixos-<version>` so
the doc doesn't bit-rot the next time Hydra rolls forward.

Both points raised by Copilot review on PR #159.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
